[[{"str":"Sentence Completion Questions Strategy Practice","x":134.19911262622878,"y":753.67506332,"width":369.82881243243827,"height":18.015113279999998},{"str":"","x":175.64735448,"y":708.63728012,"width":0,"height":14.0067505752},{"str":"The environmental impact of fashion","x":175.64735448,"y":708.63728012,"width":244.32526772271657,"height":14.0067505752},{"str":"","x":72.06045311999999,"y":674.85894272,"width":0,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"The fashion industry is one of the major polluting industries in the world. The","x":72.06045311999999,"y":674.85894272,"width":451.68557333334775,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"production and distribution of the crops, fibers and garments used in fashion all","x":72.06045311999999,"y":658.34508888,"width":451.4744588446987,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"contribute to differing forms of environmental pollution, including water, air, and soil","x":72.06045311999999,"y":641.83123504,"width":451.7969894227882,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"pollution. The textile industry is the second greatest polluter of local freshwater in the","x":72.06045311999999,"y":625.3173812,"width":451.4627301652478,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"world.","x":72.06045311999999,"y":608.80352736,"width":32.03664177272434,"height":12.01007552},{"str":" ","x":104.09709489272433,"y":608.80352736,"width":3.6562506399999974,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"Some of the main factors that contribute to this industrial pollution are the vast","x":106.84158528687735,"y":608.80352736,"width":416.82820541059635,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"","x":72.06045311999999,"y":592.28967352,"width":0,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"overproduction of fashion items, the use of synthetic fibers, and the agricultural","x":72.06045311999999,"y":592.28967352,"width":451.54483014074685,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"pollution caused by the use of fashion crops.","x":72.06045311999999,"y":575.77581968,"width":237.01719728876822,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"The quantity of new garments bought by Americans has tripled since the 1960s. This","x":72.06045311999999,"y":542.748112,"width":451.3806300696482,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"exponential increase has caused the need for more resources, and the need for a","x":72.06045311999999,"y":526.2342581600001,"width":451.2457456921381,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"speedier process in which clothes are produced. One of the main contributors to the","x":72.06045311999999,"y":509.72040432,"width":451.2164260352246,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"rapid production of pollution is the rapid production of clothes due to increased","x":72.06045311999999,"y":493.20655048000003,"width":451.1577810766617,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"consumption. Every year the world as a whole consumes more than 80 billion items","x":72.06045311999999,"y":476.69269664,"width":451.4334068452615,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"of clothing. Those clothes contribute to resource pollution and waste pollution due to","x":72.06045311999999,"y":460.17884280000004,"width":451.0874097205627,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"the fact that most of these items will one day be thrown out. People are consuming","x":72.06045311999999,"y":443.66498896,"width":451.28093689482205,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"more and they want it for cheaper prices, and the companies producing these cheap","x":72.06045311999999,"y":427.15113512000005,"width":451.73834818734883,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"items, which are making a profit, want the clothes as fast as possible. This creates a","x":72.06045311999999,"y":410.63728128,"width":451.7442163702986,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"trend called fast fashion. Fast fashion is an approach to the design, creation, and","x":72.06045311999999,"y":394.12342744000006,"width":451.73835010896113,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"marketing of clothing fashions that emphasizes making fashion trends quickly and","x":72.06045311999999,"y":377.60957360000003,"width":451.14018829768736,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"cheaply available to consumers. The idea is that speedy mass production combined","x":72.06045311999999,"y":361.09571976,"width":451.2281526129117,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"with cheap labor will make clothes cheaper for those buying them, thus leading to","x":72.06045311999999,"y":344.58186592000004,"width":451.3806282080865,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"increased sales.","x":72.06045311999999,"y":328.06801208,"width":86.78569673502284,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"The main concern with fast fashion is the clothes waste it produces. According to the","x":72.06045311999999,"y":295.0403044000001,"width":451.44513540461134,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"Environmental Protection Agency, 15.1 million tons of textile clothing waste was","x":72.06045311999999,"y":278.52645056000006,"width":451.70316256934973,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"produced in 2013 alone. When textile clothing ends up in landfills, the chemicals in","x":72.06045311999999,"y":262.01259672000003,"width":451.40408166371316,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"the clothes, such as the dye, can cause environmental problems because they","x":72.06045311999999,"y":245.49874288,"width":451.8087179220876,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"gradually seep into the ground. On top of that, there is also the issue of so much","x":72.06045311999999,"y":228.9848890400001,"width":451.37476572992296,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"used clothing waste needing to be disposed of in an ever increasing number of","x":72.06045311999999,"y":212.47103520000007,"width":451.6562519349734,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"landfill sites. Moreover, when unsold clothes are burned, a copious amount of CO2 is","x":72.06045311999999,"y":195.95718136000005,"width":451.21056373721234,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"released into the atmosphere. As per a World Resources Institute report, 1.2 billion","x":72.06045311999999,"y":179.44332752000003,"width":451.11673117898783,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"tons of CO2 is released into the atmosphere per year by the fast fashion industry. In","x":72.06045311999999,"y":162.92947368,"width":451.19883319619987,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"2019, it was announced that France was making an effort to prevent companies from","x":72.06045311999999,"y":146.4156198400001,"width":451.2985242692627,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"carrying out the practice of incinerating unsold fashion items.","x":72.06045311999999,"y":129.90176600000007,"width":322.44237765629094,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"","x":72.06045311999999,"y":96.87405832000002,"width":0,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"Now that there is a continuous increase in the amount of clothing that is consumed,","x":72.06045311999999,"y":96.87405832000002,"width":451.63279079289816,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"another issue that arises is that a lot of the clothing is no longer made from natural","x":72.06045311999999,"y":80.3602044800001,"width":451.52723730172227,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"","x":72.06045311999999,"y":44.32997792000003,"width":0,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"Note: This is not a real IELTS test. This practice test is to give you an opportunity to practise","x":72.06045311999999,"y":44.32997792000003,"width":444.120631174785,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"implementing the strategies from the course. It does not reflect the scores, time needed or","x":72.06045311999999,"y":30.068013240000028,"width":444.4724880753799,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"level of difficulty of a real IELTS test.","x":72.06045311999999,"y":15.806048560000022,"width":176.13409149452846,"height":12.01007552}],[{"str":"Sentence Completion Questions Strategy Practice","x":134.19911262622878,"y":753.67503776,"width":369.82881243243827,"height":18.015113279999998},{"str":"","x":72.06045311999999,"y":710.88914372,"width":0,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"materials and crops. Clothing used to be produced from mainly \"natural fibers\" such","x":72.06045311999999,"y":710.88914372,"width":451.21642417366274,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"as wool, cotton or silk, but nowadays inexpensive synthetic textile fibers","x":72.06045311999999,"y":694.3752898800001,"width":403.7215033461493,"height":12.01007552},{"str":" ","x":475.7819564661491,"y":694.3752898800001,"width":5.656250160000165,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"such as","x":480.02770594,"y":694.3752898800001,"width":43.63622047779841,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"","x":72.06045311999999,"y":677.8614360400001,"width":0,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"polyester or nylon are becoming increasingly common. Polyester is one of the most","x":72.06045311999999,"y":677.8614360400001,"width":451.60347137618623,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"popular fibers used in fashion today, and it is found in about 60% of garments in","x":72.06045311999999,"y":661.3475822,"width":451.6445233756236,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"retail stores, which is about 21.3 million tons of polyester. The popularity of polyester","x":72.06045311999999,"y":644.8337283600001,"width":451.5272373017225,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"keeps increasing as well, as can be seen from the fact that there was a 157 percent","x":72.06045311999999,"y":628.31987452,"width":451.36890133014697,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"increase in polyester clothing consumption from 2000 to 2015.","x":72.06045311999999,"y":611.8060206800001,"width":330.47059694836537,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"Synthetic polyester is made from a chemical reaction involving coal, petroleum, air","x":72.06045311999999,"y":578.778313,"width":451.5096389380629,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"and water. When coal is burned, it emits a large amount of carbon dioxide into the","x":72.06045311999999,"y":562.2644591600001,"width":451.7852607433376,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"atmosphere, and the use of petroleum in the process releases several air pollutants,","x":72.06045311999999,"y":545.75060532,"width":451.80871966354846,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"such as particulate matter, nitrogen oxides, carbon monoxide, hydrogen sulphide","x":72.06045311999999,"y":529.2367514800001,"width":451.74421246702394,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"and sulphur dioxide. Moreover, polyester is \"non-biodegradable\", meaning it can","x":72.06045311999999,"y":512.7228976400002,"width":451.26333853116273,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"never be converted into a state that is naturally found in the natural world. Due to all","x":72.06045311999999,"y":496.2090438,"width":451.298526250925,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"of the time and resources it takes to make polyester and it never being able to revert","x":72.06045311999999,"y":479.6951899600001,"width":451.6914319682872,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"to a state that can contribute to any natural nutrient cycles, polyester can be","x":72.06045311999999,"y":463.18133611999997,"width":451.28679570991267,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"considered energy intensive with no net gain. When polyester clothing is washed,","x":72.06045311999999,"y":446.66748228000006,"width":451.3982228486226,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"microplastics,","x":72.06045311999999,"y":430.15362844000015,"width":72.74071112359886,"height":12.01007552},{"str":" ","x":144.80116424359886,"y":430.15362844000015,"width":11.437500239999983,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"which","x":153.38649184624998,"y":430.15362844000015,"width":30.705446923699622,"height":12.01007552},{"str":" ","x":184.0919387699496,"y":430.15362844000015,"width":11.437500080000008,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"are","x":192.67726625249998,"y":430.15362844000015,"width":17.358312154899245,"height":12.01007552},{"str":" ","x":210.03557840739927,"y":430.15362844000015,"width":11.437500159999939,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"extremely","x":218.62090594999998,"y":430.15362844000015,"width":52.057343745773764,"height":12.01007552},{"str":" ","x":270.6782496957738,"y":430.15362844000015,"width":11.437497759999935,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"small","x":279.26357543686316,"y":430.15362844000015,"width":28.025464266524715,"height":12.01007552},{"str":" ","x":307.28903970338797,"y":430.15362844000015,"width":11.437502559999867,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"pieces","x":315.87436904749995,"y":430.15362844000015,"width":34.71662442989924,"height":12.01007552},{"str":" ","x":350.59099347739925,"y":430.15362844000015,"width":11.437500159999976,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"of","x":359.17632102,"y":430.15362844000015,"width":10.016215266199621,"height":12.01007552},{"str":" ","x":369.1925362861996,"y":430.15362844000015,"width":11.437500080000008,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"plastic","x":377.77786376874997,"y":430.15362844000015,"width":34.04223058587453,"height":12.01007552},{"str":" ","x":411.8200943546244,"y":430.15362844000015,"width":11.437497600000073,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"resulting","x":420.40541997561314,"y":430.15362844000015,"width":45.39550498077377,"height":12.01007552},{"str":" ","x":465.8009249563867,"y":430.15362844000015,"width":11.43750776000025,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"from","x":474.38625820377354,"y":430.15362844000015,"width":24.020150919899244,"height":12.01007552},{"str":" ","x":498.4064091236727,"y":430.15362844000015,"width":11.437500160000129,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"the","x":506.99173666627354,"y":430.15362844000015,"width":16.69564687022434,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"breakdown of consumer products, are shed and enter the water system, which leads","x":72.06045311999999,"y":413.6397746,"width":451.5448283992862,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"to micro pollution in waterways, including oceans. Due to the small size of the micro","x":72.06045311999999,"y":397.1259207600001,"width":451.33371006741265,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"pollutants, it is easy for fish within waterways to absorb them in their body fat. The","x":72.06045311999999,"y":380.61206691999996,"width":451.7442125270742,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"fish can then be consumed by humans, and these humans will also absorb the","x":72.06045311999999,"y":364.09821308000005,"width":451.8028555039743,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"polyester micro pollutants in the fish in a process called biomagnification.","x":72.06045311999999,"y":347.58435924000014,"width":387.19005516586526,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"","x":72.06045311999999,"y":314.5566515600001,"width":0,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"While synthetic fibers have a significant negative impact on the environment, natural","x":72.06045311999999,"y":314.5566515600001,"width":451.8028535223119,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"fibers also contribute to pollution through agricultural pollution. Cotton production","x":72.06045311999999,"y":298.04279771999995,"width":451.16951335913495,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"requires a large amount of pesticides and water usage. Cotton is considered the","x":72.06045311999999,"y":281.52894388000004,"width":451.4744550014745,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"world's dirtiest crop because it uses 16% of the world's pesticides. Two of the main","x":72.06045311999999,"y":265.01509004000013,"width":451.08154538083755,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"ingredients in pesticides are nitrates and phosphates. When the pesticides leak into","x":72.06045311999999,"y":248.5012362,"width":451.49791031866266,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"stream systems surrounding the cropland, the nitrates and phosphates contribute to","x":72.06045311999999,"y":231.98738236000008,"width":451.32198150806306,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"water eutrophication. Water eutrophication is an environmental phenomenon that","x":72.06045311999999,"y":215.47352852000017,"width":451.6738391292626,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"causes a depletion of oxygen when the nutrient overload from pesticides causes a","x":72.06045311999999,"y":198.95967468000003,"width":451.65625007341185,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"boom in plant growth and death. As regards wool, it is made from the fur of sheep,","x":72.06045311999999,"y":182.44582084000012,"width":451.52137302204744,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"and sheep are ruminants and hence produce methane, which is a very potent","x":72.06045311999999,"y":165.931967,"width":451.7324819860617,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"greenhouse gas. The same problem exists for leather as cattle are ruminants too.","x":72.06045311999999,"y":149.41811316000008,"width":451.28093701492287,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"For","x":72.06045311999999,"y":132.90425932000016,"width":18.015113159899244,"height":12.01007552},{"str":" ","x":90.07556627989923,"y":132.90425932000016,"width":11.437500159999995,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"temperate","x":98.66089382249999,"y":132.90425932000016,"width":54.07466099817302,"height":12.01007552},{"str":" ","x":152.73555482067306,"y":132.90425932000016,"width":10.43749791999994,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"zones,","x":160.5702509618632,"y":132.90425932000016,"width":35.38515399424906,"height":12.01007552},{"str":" ","x":195.95540495611226,"y":132.90425932000016,"width":10.437505199999958,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"linen,","x":203.79010656188677,"y":132.90425932000016,"width":28.711586669899244,"height":12.01007552},{"str":" ","x":232.50169323178605,"y":132.90425932000016,"width":10.437500159999969,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"which","x":240.33639105438678,"y":132.90425932000016,"width":30.705446923699622,"height":12.01007552},{"str":" ","x":271.04183797808645,"y":132.90425932000016,"width":10.437500079999925,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"is","x":278.87653574063677,"y":132.90425932000016,"width":8.673291857825093,"height":12.01007552},{"str":" ","x":287.5498275984619,"y":132.90425932000016,"width":10.437502479999965,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"made","x":295.38452716252357,"y":132.90425932000016,"width":30.042781518923963,"height":12.01007552},{"str":" ","x":325.4273086814476,"y":132.90425932000016,"width":10.437492719999936,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"from","x":333.2620009193632,"y":132.90425932000016,"width":24.020150919899244,"height":12.01007552},{"str":" ","x":357.28215183926244,"y":132.90425932000016,"width":10.437500159999969,"height":12.01007552},{"str":"flax,","x":365.11684966186317,"y":132.904